      "statistics": {},
      "description": "Watch Inter vs Real Betis highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. Inter and Real Betis faced off in a pre-season friendly that served as a crucial test for both squads' fitness and tactical cohesion. The match offered a glimpse into the preparations of both sides as they gear up for their respective domestic campaigns. Tactical Battle in the Summer Heat On August 15, 2026 , Inter hosted Real Betis in a high-profile Friendly encounter. Both teams looked to find their rhythm early on, resulting in a cautious first half that focused heavily on defensive structure and midfield duels. While both sides showed glimpses of quality, the final ball often lacked the necessary precision to break the deadlock during the opening 45 minutes. Stones Secures the Breakthrough The intensity rose in the second half as substitutions altered the flow of the game. In the 65th minute, F. P. Esposito was shown a yellow card as the physical nature of the contest intensified. Just as a stalemate seemed the most likely outcome, the breakthrough arrived in the 82nd minute. John Stones found the back of the net to give Inter a 1-0 lead, capitalising on a late surge of pressure. Real Betis pushed hard for a late equalizer, but their efforts were met by a resolute Italian defense. The frustration of the Spanish side became evident in stoppage time when Natan received a yellow card in the 90+4th minute, effectively ending their hopes of a comeback in this tightly contested match."
